msgid ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: A quickstart guide for the pauli-prop Qiskit addons package\n"
msgstr ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: Isang quickstart na gabay para sa pauli-prop na Qiskit addons package\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide we use the ``pauli-prop`` package to classically simulate the time dynamics of a 10-qubit kicked Ising model on a 1D spin chain.\n"
msgstr "Sa gabay na ito, gagamitin natin ang ``pauli-prop`` package para i-simulate nang classical ang time dynamics ng isang 10-qubit na kicked Ising model sa 1D spin chain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the inputs for Pauli propagation {#prepare-the-inputs-for-pauli-propagation}"
msgstr "Ihanda ang mga input para sa Pauli propagation {#prepare-the-inputs-for-pauli-propagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr "Ang Hamiltonian na isinasaalang-alang ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and $h$ is the global transverse field. A first-order Trotter decomposition of the time-evolved operator will be implemented as a quantum circuit, $U$, over $20$ Trotter steps. The coupling constant, $J$, will be fixed at $J=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, and $h$ will be fixed at $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. The $ZZ$ interactions will be implemented using Clifford gates ($CX$, $Sdg$, $\\sqrt{Y}$).\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $J>0$ ay naglalarawan ng coupling ng mga magkatabing spin, $i<j$, at ang $h$ ay ang global na transverse field. Ang first-order na Trotter decomposition ng time-evolved na operator ay ipapatupad bilang isang quantum circuit, $U$, sa loob ng $20$ Trotter step. Ang coupling constant, $J$, ay ifi-fix sa $J=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, at ang $h$ ay ifi-fix sa $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Ang mga interaksyong $ZZ$ ay ipapatupad gamit ang mga Clifford gate ($CX$, $Sdg$, $\\sqrt{Y}$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We implement the Trotterized time evolution as a quantum circuit and use $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ for the non-Clifford rotations about the x-axis. The further these angles are from Clifford angles (for example, $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), the more difficult the system will be to simulate for Pauli propagation methods.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad natin ang Trotterized na time evolution bilang isang quantum circuit at gumagamit ng $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ para sa mga non-Clifford na rotation sa paligid ng x-axis. Habang lumalayo ang mga anggulong ito sa mga Clifford angle (halimbawa, $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), mas nagiging mahirap i-simulate ang sistema gamit ang mga Pauli propagation method.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the choice of observable, we consider the average single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, where $N$ is the number of spins.\n"
msgstr "Para sa pagpili ng observable, isinasaalang-alang natin ang average na single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, kung saan ang $N$ ay ang bilang ng mga spin.\n"

