# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the time evolution of the system with Pauli propagation {#simulate-the-time-evolution-of-the-system-with-pauli-propagation}"
msgstr "I-simulate ang time evolution ng sistema gamit ang Pauli propagation {#simulate-the-time-evolution-of-the-system-with-pauli-propagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have our circuit, $U$, and observable, $O$, we can easily simulate the system in a few steps:\n"
msgstr "Kapag mayroon na tayong circuit, $U$, at observable, $O$, madali nating mai-simulate ang sistema sa ilang hakbang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separate $U$, into its Clifford, $C$, and non-Clifford, $P$, parts such that $U=PC$ using ``evolve_through_cliffords``\n"
msgstr "Hatiin ang $U$ sa Clifford na bahagi nito, $C$, at non-Clifford na bahagi, $P$, para ang $U=PC$, gamit ang ``evolve_through_cliffords``\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagate $O$ through $P$, resulting in a new operator, $O^\\prime$, using ``pauli_prop.propagate_through_circuit``\n"
msgstr "I-propagate ang $O$ sa pamamagitan ng $P$, na magreresulta sa bagong operator, $O^\\prime$, gamit ang ``pauli_prop.propagate_through_circuit``\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evolve $O^\\prime$ through the Clifford part of the circuit using the Clifford evolution support built into Qiskit\n"
msgstr "I-evolve ang $O^\\prime$ sa Clifford na bahagi ng circuit gamit ang suporta sa Clifford evolution na built-in sa Qiskit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Approximate the expectation value as $\\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle \\approx \\langle0|U^\\dagger OU|0\\rangle$ by summing the coefficients in $O^\\prime$ associated with fully-diagonal Pauli terms (Pauli terms containing either ``I`` or ``Z`` on all qubits). Remember, this is an approximation because we truncated terms from $O^\\prime$ as we propagated it through the non-Clifford part of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Tantiyahin ang expectation value bilang $\\langle0|O^\\prime|0\\rangle \\approx \\langle0|U^\\dagger OU|0\\rangle$ sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama-sama ng mga coefficient sa $O^\\prime$ na nauugnay sa mga fully-diagonal na Pauli term (mga Pauli term na naglalaman ng ``I`` o ``Z`` sa lahat ng qubit). Tandaan, isa itong approximation dahil nag-truncate tayo ng mga term mula sa $O^\\prime$ habang pina-propagate ito sa non-Clifford na bahagi ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we run larger calculations, the expectation value approximations become more accurate. In this example, we saturate the full Pauli space at around $4^{10}\\approx10^6$, which is reflected in the curve flattening out between the final two points.\n"
msgstr "Habang nagpapatakbo tayo ng mas malalaking kalkulasyon, mas nagiging tumpak ang mga approximation ng expectation value. Sa halimbawang ito, napupuno natin ang buong Pauli space sa humigit-kumulang $4^{10}\\approx10^6$, na makikita sa pagpapatag ng kurba sa pagitan ng huling dalawang punto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the plot below shows a monotonic convergence, Pauli propagation simulations do not generally converge monotonically. It is not unusual to see \"bumpy\" behavior in these types of plots.\n"
msgstr "Bagama't monotonic ang convergence na ipinapakita ng plot sa ibaba, karaniwang hindi monotonic ang convergence ng mga Pauli propagation simulation. Hindi kakaiba na makakita ng \"bumpy\" na behavior sa ganitong uri ng mga plot.\n"

